What is in this directory, and why it is not in `data/`.

These files hold this project's own conclusions: what the measurements and the
published tables were read to mean. A file here names a structure, fits a
topology, gives a coefficient a range, or says which of several readings the
evidence leaves standing. None of that is a measurement.

They are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The dedication is the same as `data/LICENSE` and the reason for the separate
file is not a legal one. `data/` holds what a unit answered, and a consumer that
harvests that directory must not pick up an interpretation along with it. The
separation is what makes the two distinguishable without reading any prose:
different directory, different schema, different index.

Every claim here rests on records under `data/` and rows under `documents/`, and
says which. The references run one way only -- an inference cites a record, and
no record cites an inference. A reader who disagrees with a conclusion here can
delete this directory and still have the archive.

A citation is welcome. It is not a condition.
